# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# CCE — Capital Control Engine
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Documentation
# Most of the 18-document spec set stays local: publishing all of it makes
# the repo harder to read, not easier. The five below carry the argument a
# reviewer actually needs - what it is, how it is layered, what the controls
# are, what the maths is, and what the safety invariants are.
#
# NOTE: must be `docs/*` not `docs/` — git cannot re-include a file whose
# parent DIRECTORY is excluded, so the negations below would be silently
# ignored under a `docs/` rule.
docs/*
!docs/CLAUDE.md
!docs/01-PRODUCT-SPECIFICATION.md
!docs/02-ARCHITECTURE.md
!docs/07-RISK-POLICY.md
!docs/08-FINANCIAL-METHODS.md
!docs/10-RULES.md
# ── Secrets ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
# ...but the TEMPLATE is committed: a fresh clone otherwise has no
# record of which variables exist, and the constitution requires it.
# It holds no secrets — only defaults and a commented-out placeholder.
!.env.example
.streamlit/secrets.toml
*.pem
*.key

# ── Database (recreatable from migrations) ───────────────────
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
data/cce.db

# ── Market data ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# raw/ and processed/ are regenerable; cache/ is COMMITTED so the
# demo is reproducible and runs with no network. See docs/02 §8.
data/raw/
data/processed/
!data/cache/
!data/cache/**

